// A 12-bar solo in box 1 of A minor pentatonic over A7 | D7 | E7, swung 8ths. Bars 1-2 are the
// main phrase; bar 3 is a variant of bar 1 and bars 7-8 repeat 1-2, so seven bars are new. Whole-step
// bends are on the plain string 2. Each phrase lands on a note of the chord under it.
\title "12-bar solo in A, box 1"
\tempo 80
\track ("Guitar" "Gtr.") { instrument acousticguitarsteel }
\staff { tabs }
\ts (4 4) \tf t8
:4 8.2{lf 4 b (0 4) txt "A7"} :8 5.2{lf 2} 5.1{lf 2} :2 5.2{lf 2 v} |
:8 8.2{lf 5} 5.2{lf 2} 7.3{lf 4} 5.3{lf 2} :2 7.4{lf 4 v} |
:4 8.2{lf 4 b (0 4)} :8 5.2{lf 2} 5.1{lf 2} :2 8.1{lf 5 v} |
:8 8.1{lf 5 h} 5.1{lf 2} 8.2{lf 5} 5.2{lf 2} 7.3{lf 4} 5.3{lf 2} :4 5.4{lf 2} |
:8 5.4{lf 2 txt "D7"} 7.4{lf 4} 5.3{lf 2 h} 7.3{lf 4} :2 5.5{lf 2 v} |
:4 8.2{lf 4 b (0 4 4 0)} :8 5.3{lf 2} 7.4{lf 4} :2 5.5{lf 2} |
:4 8.2{lf 4 b (0 4) txt "A7"} :8 5.2{lf 2} 5.1{lf 2} :2 5.2{lf 2 v} |
